ITEM 5. L4-E12's SGP41 shutdown on a TMP117 (v2/vendor/ti/ti-tmp117-temperature.pdf)
   p.1: '+-0.15 C (maximum) from -40 C to 70 C' (SNOSD82D, revised September 2022; the sheet prints the minus as an en dash)
   p.6, 6.5 Electrical Characteristics, TMP117 row -40 to 70 C: MIN -0.15, TYP +-0.05, MAX 0.15 C, over free-air temperature;
     conditions: 8 averages, 1-Hz conversion cycle, thermal pad unsoldered (DRV), I2C inputs VIL <= 0.05 V+, VIH >= 0.95 V+;
     the TMP117N rows print +-0.2 C from -40 to 100 C (no +-0.15 C row); board B's part is TMP117AIDRVR (gen_sch_b.py)
   L4-E12's lag (l4e12_thermal.py): READ_S 1 s and TAU_S 60 s, 'a reading every second; a sensor's thermal time constant in the case's moving air'
   the lag: 15.0 K/h x 61 s = 0.254167 K (the record: 0.254167 K)
   off at 55 - 0.15 - 0.5 - lag = 54.095833 C, set at 54.0 C; the SGP41 then at most 54.904167 C (the record: 54.095833, 54.904167 C)
   on and used at 50 - 0.15 - 0.5 - lag = 49.095833 C, set at 49.0 C; at most 49.904167 C while used (the record: 49.095833, 49.904167 C)
   break-even of the 54.0 C setting at +-0.15 C: the sensor-to-SGP41 time constant at most 83.0 s at 15 K/h (the record assumes 60 s); off point 54.095833 C
   break-even of the 54.0 C setting at +-0.20 C: the sensor-to-SGP41 time constant at most 71.0 s at 15 K/h (the record assumes 60 s); off point 54.045833 C
   the register (set 27): R-146 carries the 0.5 K placement (yes); R-139 now names the lag: yes
     R-139's acceptance: 'the SGP41's shutdown lag measured on the bench, from the TMP117's reading crossing 54.0 C to the part's off
     state, at most the 61 s assumed'
   what that interval holds: the reading period and the firmware's and the switch's response, about 1 s of the 61 s;
     the 60 s thermal time constant lies BEFORE the reading crosses 54.0 C (the reading lags the SGP41 by rate x TAU_S = 0.250000 K),
     so the measurement cannot see it, and passes while the time constant it should bound goes untested
   what would test it: the TMP117's reading against a reference thermocouple at the SGP41 on a ramp of at least 15 K/h, the reading
     at most 0.254167 K behind it at 54.0 C (the time constant at most 60 s; the 54.0 C setting holds to 83.0 s)

